<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaEyeColours.xml                         Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-10
  ============================================================================

  WHY
  ===
  Star Wars Xenotypes ships exactly two "huge" (Jawa-style) eye genes:
      RimMandrake_Eyes_HugeYellow   tex Pawn/HeadAttachments/bigeyes/jawaeyes_yellow
      guy762_Eyes_HugeRed      tex Pawn/HeadAttachments/bigeyes/jawaeyes_red
  Two colours is thin for a whole colony of Jawa. These add orange and amber so
  the founding crew can be told apart at a glance.

  HOW
  ===
  Cloned from RimMandrake_Eyes_HugeYellow verbatim (Star Wars Xenotypes,
  1.6/Defs/GeneDefs/GeneDefs_Eyes.xml) and re-tinted with <color> rather than
  new art, so they keep the exact huge-glowing-eye silhouette that reads as a
  Jawa. Everything else is byte-identical to the donor: anchorTag, side,
  drawSize 0.2, layer 55, offset (0,0,-0.25), the West flip handling, and
  ParentName GeneEyeColor.

  ⚠️ TINT, NOT REPAINT. <color> multiplies against the existing texture. The
  donor art is already saturated yellow, so these will read as warm shifts, not
  as pure orange/amber. If they come out muddy the fallback is to point texPath
  at the art the mod already ships instead:
      Pawn/HeadAttachments/bigeyes/bigeyes_orange   (a different, "big" style)
      Pawn/HeadAttachments/bigeyes/jawaeyes_red     (correct "huge" style)

  GLOW  [added 2026-08-11]
  ======================
  Two changes, both needed. Jawa eyes are supposed to be two lights in the dark,
  not orange paint.

  1. NEW TEXTURE. Textures/RimMandrakeSW/Jawa/jawaeyes_glow.png, generated from the donor
     by pushing the core toward white and darkening the rim to 62%. Because the
     gene tints by MULTIPLY, a white core resolves to the full saturated tint
     colour while the rim resolves darker, so the falloff reads as emission.
     The original was flat (255,255,0) across the whole ellipse, which is why a
     <color> tint could only ever look like paint. Silhouette and the dark
     outline are preserved pixel for pixel; only the interior was regraded.

  2. SHADER. PawnRenderNodeProperties carries a shaderTypeDef field (confirmed
     in Verse via IL — it does not appear in a live def dump because it is null
     by default).

     ⚠️ SETTLED 2026-08-11, commit 263e539. ALL THREE JAWA EYE GENES USE
     MoteGlow. DO NOT RE-SPREAD THEM ACROSS SHADERS.

         RimMandrake_Jawa_Eyes_HugeOrange   MoteGlow
         RimMandrake_Jawa_Eyes_HugeAmber    MoteGlow
         RimMandrake_Eyes_HugeYellow MoteGlow   (set in Patches/JawaEyeGlow_Stock.xml)

     These genes DID once carry three different shaders, so one load could score
     them side by side. That load happened. MoteGlowPulseLow renders too dim to
     see at all on a pawn render node, and MoteGlowPulse was reported "so subtle
     I can't really tell" after two loads of trying — a per-pawn phase offset and
     a floored trough need C#, which a global sine in a shader cannot fake. The
     Mote shaders are additive and ignore light entirely, which is what makes
     MoteGlow work here despite being written for motes.

     TransparentPostLight is the FALLBACK, not a fourth variant to try. It draws
     after the lighting pass, so the eyes stay full brightness in pitch dark
     without being additive. Use it only if MoteGlow reads as a white blob, and
     then move all three genes together.

     What IS still open is drawSize 0.16 and whether two adjacent eyes read as
     two lights rather than one orange bar. See NEXT_RELOAD.md item V4.

  ⚠️ Only works because Jawa are EXCLUDED from Facial Animation. FA deletes the
  vanilla head draw and paints its own face, and the LFS eyes mod demonstrates
  the consequence: its FA compat patch strips renderNodeProperties off every one
  of its own eye genes. A gene can only draw its own eyes on a pawn FA is not
  drawing.

  USAGE
  =====
  These ARE added to MandrakeJawa by Patches/JawaAppearance_Tuning.xml (the patch
  named BTD_Jawa until 2026-08-19; that def no longer loads), and RimWorld
  will roll between them per pawn.

  Corrected 2026-08-10: an earlier version of this note claimed a XenotypeDef
  has a fixed gene list and cannot randomise. Wrong. GeneEyeColor is Abstract
  with exclusionTags EyeColor, so its children are mutually exclusive, and
  listing several on one xenotype makes the engine pick one. The same mod family
  already relies on this: guy762_xenotype_hutt lists four big-eye colours.

  They remain individually assignable in Character Editor for the five authored
  founding Jawa in jawa_crew_personas.md.

  ⚠️ Do NOT edit a non-human pawn's HEAD in Character Editor. Confirmed
  2026-08-10: doing so destroys the head on Mon Calamari and Bith. Eye and gene
  edits are fine; the head selector is not.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GeneDef ParentName="GeneEyeColor">
    <defName>RimMandrake_Jawa_Eyes_HugeOrange</defName>
    <label>orange huge eyes</label>
    <labelShortAdj>big-eyed</labelShortAdj>
    <description>Carriers of this gene have huge orange eyes that catch the light in the dark.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_BigYellowEyes</iconPath>
    <displayOrderInCategory>1775</displayOrderInCategory>
    <renderNodeProperties>
      <li Class="PawnRenderNodeProperties_Eye">
        <texPath>RimMandrakeSW/Jawa/jawaeyes_glow</texPath>
        <shaderTypeDef>MoteGlow</shaderTypeDef>
        <color>(255, 130, 20)</color>
        <anchorTag>RightEye</anchorTag>
        <rotDrawMode>Fresh, Rotting</rotDrawMode>
        <parentTagDef>Head</parentTagDef>
        <drawSize>0.16</drawSize>
        <side>Right</side>
        <drawData>
          <defaultData>
            <layer>55</layer>
            <offset>(0, 0, -0.25)</offset>
          </defaultData>
        </drawData>
      </li>
      <li Class="PawnRenderNodeProperties_Eye">
        <texPath>RimMandrakeSW/Jawa/jawaeyes_glow</texPath>
        <shaderTypeDef>MoteGlow</shaderTypeDef>
        <color>(255, 130, 20)</color>
        <anchorTag>LeftEye</anchorTag>
        <rotDrawMode>Fresh, Rotting</rotDrawMode>
        <parentTagDef>Head</parentTagDef>
        <drawSize>0.16</drawSize>
        <side>Left</side>
        <drawData>
          <defaultData>
            <layer>55</layer>
            <offset>(0, 0, -0.25)</offset>
            <flip>true</flip>
          </defaultData>
          <dataWest>
            <flip>false</flip>
          </dataWest>
        </drawData>
      </li>
    </renderNodeProperties>
  </GeneDef>

  <GeneDef ParentName="GeneEyeColor">
    <defName>RimMandrake_Jawa_Eyes_HugeAmber</defName>
    <label>amber huge eyes</label>
    <labelShortAdj>big-eyed</labelShortAdj>
    <description>Carriers of this gene have huge amber eyes, deep and slow to blink.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_BigYellowEyes</iconPath>
    <displayOrderInCategory>1776</displayOrderInCategory>
    <renderNodeProperties>
      <li Class="PawnRenderNodeProperties_Eye">
        <texPath>RimMandrakeSW/Jawa/jawaeyes_glow</texPath>
        <shaderTypeDef>MoteGlow</shaderTypeDef>
        <color>(255, 191, 0)</color>
        <anchorTag>RightEye</anchorTag>
        <rotDrawMode>Fresh, Rotting</rotDrawMode>
        <parentTagDef>Head</parentTagDef>
        <drawSize>0.16</drawSize>
        <side>Right</side>
        <drawData>
          <defaultData>
            <layer>55</layer>
            <offset>(0, 0, -0.25)</offset>
          </defaultData>
        </drawData>
      </li>
      <li Class="PawnRenderNodeProperties_Eye">
        <texPath>RimMandrakeSW/Jawa/jawaeyes_glow</texPath>
        <shaderTypeDef>MoteGlow</shaderTypeDef>
        <color>(255, 191, 0)</color>
        <anchorTag>LeftEye</anchorTag>
        <rotDrawMode>Fresh, Rotting</rotDrawMode>
        <parentTagDef>Head</parentTagDef>
        <drawSize>0.16</drawSize>
        <side>Left</side>
        <drawData>
          <defaultData>
            <layer>55</layer>
            <offset>(0, 0, -0.25)</offset>
            <flip>true</flip>
          </defaultData>
          <dataWest>
            <flip>false</flip>
          </dataWest>
        </drawData>
      </li>
    </renderNodeProperties>
  </GeneDef>

</Defs>
